    Tutorial: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9ad89dc61c0200941a278363ac1f0be0, type: 2}
  - Heading:
      m_Untranslated: Optimizing CAD Data with Asset Transformer Toolkit
    Text:
      m_Untranslated: <br>In this tutorial, you'll install Unity's Asset Transformer
        Toolkit (ATT), import a CAD model, adjust its import settings for accurate
        geometry and metadata, and add the resulting Prefab to your scene.
    Type: 0
    Url: 
    Metadata: 
    Image: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 36d536f14b0ceaf45aaff335c5443c14, type: 3}
    Tutorial: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 64fcebeb821d51f47a7ee14b2d57ceeb, type: 2}
  - Heading:
      m_Untranslated: Automating Fixes with Rule Sets
    Text:
      m_Untranslated: To save time on future imports, you can create a reusable ruleset
        that automatically applies your import and optimization settings. In previous
        steps, you manually adjusted the CAD model to prepare it for use in Unity.
        A Rule Set eliminates that repetition by applying those adjustments for you.
    Type: 0
    Url: 
    Metadata: 
    Image: {fileID: 2800000, guid: b408fa5807e87f4408b16c7efa033b79, type: 3}
    Tutorial: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 203ee942d10c98c4f90f33c12666ecf2, type: 2}
  - Heading:
      m_Untranslated: Finalizing the application
    Text:
      m_Untranslated: "In this tutorial, you\u2019ll connect your robot to key runtime
        systems \u2014 including the Dashboard UI, control modes, and visual feedback.
        You\u2019ll test its behavior, manage its state, and use it in a simulation
        environment we\u2019ve prepared for you."
    Type: 0
